# Things in the winery and its cellars that open a scene: the founder's cask, where Davian hid the last stone.

~ founders_cask
Narrator: The founder's cask is older than the house: black oak, bound in iron gone brown, so big a man could stand up inside it. The druids have chopped at every cask in the cellar except this one, because it was too much trouble.
if flag.winery_stone_hiding_told
* Turn the third hoop and pull. -> open_cask
* Leave it for now. -> END
else
* [Investigation DC 14] Something's wrong with the end of this cask. -> find_cask | miss_cask
* Leave it. -> END
endif

~ find_cask
Narrator: The end sounds wrong when you knock: higher, emptier, a door rather than a wall. The third hoop down turns a quarter-inch further than any hoop should.
-> open_cask

~ miss_cask
Narrator: An old cask, and a great one. If it's hiding anything, it's better at hiding than you are at finding.
-> END

~ open_cask
set winery_stone_recovered
Narrator: The hoop turns with a grudging click, and the whole end of the cask swings out on hidden pins. Inside, wrapped in a wine-stained shirt, lies a stone as green as a leaf held up to the sun, and faintly warm.
if guest:adrian_martikov
Adrian: The founder's cask. Of course. He told Stefania and not me. Of course he did.
endif
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Now that is a hiding place. I'd have looked under the floor. So did the druids, by the state of it.
interject class:wizard: There's an enchantment in it: old, patient, very simple. Grow. Whoever made it wanted nothing else from the world.
-> END
